content.text:
pickUpgrade: if claim is in reward modal, no extra. But after pick, maybe show region claim details already. Fine. Need ensure state after reward. Add no changes except maybe `this.ui.tutorialEvent('boon')` not necessary.

Now add dungeon methods, war map, shop, prologue/tutorial wrappers. Place after showVictory or before hero. Let's add around after `keepBuilding()`. Need snapshot capture similar to beginWave. We'll write:

```js
dungeonAvailable(d) { return this.wavesSurvived >= d.unlockWave; }
openWarMap() { if (this.state==='combat') { toast...; return; } this.ui.tutorialEvent('map'); this.ui.showWarMap(this.mapSelected); }
openShop() {...}
closeOverlay() maybe.
startDungeon(id) { ... }
onDungeonComplete(d) {...}
finishDungeon() {...}
retryDungeon() {...}
```

Snapshot helper duplication: create `takeSnapshot()` and use beginWave too? Not necessary but we can add for dungeon. In startDungeon:
```
if (!this.dungeonAvailable(d)) toast
if (this.state !== 'build') ...
this.clearSelection(); close modal; tool camera; snapshot = {...}
this.saveNow();
this.state='combat'; activeDungeon=d; cooldowns reset; combat.startDungeon(d, this.combatBonuses()); ui.enterCombat(); ui.enterDungeon(d); audio wave/horn; ui.callout(d.power.toUpperCase(), d.name, d.bossLine, 'boss'); ...
```
`ui.enterCombat()` then `ui.enterDungeon(d)` to set labels. We'll implement in UI.
- snapshot should include activeDungeon? Snapshot for retry is pre-dungeon city state; we store `dungeonId`.
- `onDungeonComplete(d)`:
```
if (this.state!=='combat' || this.activeDungeon?.id !== d.id) return;
combat.active=false; state='reward'; wavesSurvived? Dungeons should not increase wave progression. But unlock based wavesSurvived, keep.
const first = !this.clearedDungeons.includes(d.id);
let loot = {...d.loot};
if (!first) { for keys except crowns half } 
grant loot; if first -> push cleared, add crown loot already in loot? d.loot includes crowns; addCrowns separately instead of grant resources. We'll split crowns.
if first: premium.ownedSkins.push(d.skin); savePremium; saveNow.
this.activeDungeon = d; // keep for modal
this.castle.repairAll(0.35);
this.updateRank(true); checkQuests(true); audio.victory; shake(.3);
this.ui.showDungeonComplete(d, {first, loot, skin});
this.saveDirty = true;
```
- Note loot includes crowns; `grant` would add resources.crowns incorrectly. Split.
- `finishDungeon()`: state='build'; combat.clear(); activeDungeon=null; ui.setBuildMode(); controls; saveNow; updateRank.
- `retryDungeon()`: restore snapshot then startDungeon(id) but restore sets state build and closes modal. Then startDungeon(id) opens combat. Need avoid snapshot overwritten pre-dungeon? `startDungeon` will capture snapshot again from restored state, fine. `restoreSnapshot` currently doesn't know activeDungeon. Add `this.activeDungeon=null` at end. Then call ui.closeModal(true) and startDungeon.
- `onDefeat` dynamic with dungeon; `ui.showDefeat(!!this.activeDungeon)`.

- `openWarMap` while paused? state paused -> modal is pause; opening war map replaces it. `openWarMap` should set `this.previousState`? It can just show map; on close, it calls closeModal; state remains paused. But `escapeModal` in UI when g.state==='paused' calls g.resume(), so closing map while paused would resume game. That's acceptable? Better map from pause should return to pause or resume. Simpler: in showPause, the "War Map" button calls `g.pauseReturn = ...`? Let's keep map accessible only in build/sandbox and from title (via button we might add). In pause, add War Map button that closes and `g.resume(); g.openWarMap();`. That works: resume then open map. Similarly shop from pause: resume then openShop.
- `openShop` if combat return; if paused: `this.resume();`.
- for state title, shop/map could open but HUD hidden. Perhaps allow; map march would need start campaign. We can just require state build/sandbox; from pause we resume.

Let's add methods.

